C('8-020',[34],'J156-8-05','6-59','Magasins triviaux ... tout ensemble ordonné','Every poset M gives a trivial magasin by ≪°=identity and interior disjointness=inequality; ≪=≤, all elements are compatible, and figures are lower sets. Triviality is equivalent to universal compatibility, to M itself being a figure, and to disjointness of every distinct pair. Having ≪=≤ alone is weaker. Mog L1 holds for this example iff the poset is discrete.','proof sketched','order')
C('8-021',[35,36],'J156-8-05','73-145','Pour que φ:I→M définisse une figure indexée','An indexed figure is equivalently an injective monotone map φ:I→M inducing an order isomorphism on every principal lower set and taking unequal indices to interior-disjoint elements. Its image is then a lower compatible subset and φ an order isomorphism onto it. The polyhedral condition is exactly the corresponding meet condition on I.','proved there','order')
C('8-022',[36,37,38],'J156-8-05','148-261','conditions a), c), d) ... φ(F)∈Fig(M′)','A map preserving incidence, open refinement, and interior disjointness, and inducing bijections on principal face sets, sends figures to figures injectively on each figure; preserves compatibility, disjointness, compatible unions/intersections, refinement and induced restriction; it reflects incidence/disjointness inside any one figure. A later marginal note dated 11/12 July explicitly says face-bijection condition d) should be optional for general comorphisms. The theorem remains stated with d), while the definition is loosened.','corrected by himself later (both places)','morphisms')
C('8-023',[38,39,40,41],'J156-8-05','271-429','Mulomb ... Mais l’inverse est-il tjrs vrai','The full multishadow map M→Figel(M) preserves interior disjointness because a common open refinement would contradict irreflexivity. Its converse is not general: distinct lieux can lack a common open refinement yet fail to be disjoint. The extra class with disjointness defined as absence of a common ≪°-lower bound is described by the two orders plus carrier axioms. The lieux multishadow map requires Mog L1. A surjective set map induces an injective comorphism on set-theoretic elementary figures.','proof sketched','morphisms')
C('8-024',[42,43,44,45],'J156-8-06','5-130','fonction genre support ... (ii bis) ... (ii ter)','For a proposed support X↦|X|⊆P, require refinement-monotonicity, nonempty interiors, disjointness reflection, covering and point separation. The additional requirement that faces of each X form an indexed set-theoretic figure is equivalent to |X| being partitioned by its face interiors; with it, support inclusion among faces reflects incidence. These are axioms/criteria for support representations, not a theorem asserting every magasin has such a faithful P.','proved there','support')
C('8-025',[46,47,48,49,50,51,52],'J156-8-06','165-377','Conditions équivalentes ... I^x a un plus petit élément','For a monotone family (X_i) indexed by a poset I, put X_i°=X_i∖⋃_{j<i}X_j. Equivalent conditions: every nonempty membership set I^x has a least element; every I^x has a minimal element and X_i∩X_j=⋃_{k≤i,j}X_k; the interiors are disjoint and X_i=⋃_{j≤i}X_j°; or the nonempty interiors partition the support, each X_i is saturated, and X_j°⊆X_i with nonempty X_j° implies j≤i. With every interior nonempty, i↦X_i is an order embedding and an indexed figure. The proof of the second equivalence continues through scans 50–51, and the local figure corollary through 52.','proved there','order')
C('8-026',[53,54],'J156-8-07','153-236','contreexemple ... il manque N','For an infinite decreasing chain A_n with nonempty intersection N and an incomparable A∞ meeting A0 exactly in N, interiors can partition the total support without each A_n being their union over lower indices; saturation fails. Adding A=A∞∖N restores saturation but still does not make interior inclusion reflect the indexing order: A∞°=N⊂A_n while A∞⊄A_n. These refute the questions on scans47,53–54, not the fully hypothesized proposition.','proved there','order','Recomputed symbolically in computations.py: A_n={ω}∪{k∈N:k≥n}, A∞={ω,q}, A={q}; the general set identities and witnesses are printed. The i−1 in scan54 is inconsistent and flagged.')
C('8-027',[55,56,57],'J156-8-07','241-332','f*(Φ)={f⁻¹(A) ... f⁻¹(A°)≠∅}','Every set map f:L′→L pulls back set-theoretic figures by retaining precisely strata whose interiors meet the image. Factoring through image L0 separates restriction, change of ambient set, and surjective inverse image. For an inclusion i, i*i_*=id, i_*i*(X)=i_*(1)·X, and i_*(X′)·Y=i_*(X′·i*(Y)). Inverse image preserves total support and complements; inclusion direct image generally does not. Both preserve arbitrary existing inclusion joins; direct image preserves nonempty inclusion meets.','proof sketched','sheaf')
P('8-06','Appropriate comorphisms and optional face lifting',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':36,'file':'J156-8-05','lines':'168-183'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':37,'file':'J156-8-05','lines':'192-208'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':38,'file':'J156-8-05','lines':'263-269'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':41,'file':'J156-8-05','lines':'422'}],'How strong should comorphisms be? Condition d) ought to remain optional; the force of disjointness preservation is unclear.','Separate structure-preserving maps, figure-preserving maps, and face-bijective maps; characterize each by explicit preservation properties rather than treating the draft definitions as interchangeable.')
P('8-07','Representing supports by sets',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':42,'file':'J156-8-06','lines':'5-46'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':43,'file':'J156-8-06','lines':'52-77'}],'Find support functions and decide whether support inclusion recovers the face order.','Under the partition condition the incidence-reflection lemma is proved here; existence and universality of a sufficiently faithful support representation require the later disjunctor construction.')
P('8-08','General quotient by an interior-disjointness support',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':56,'file':'J156-8-07','lines':'289-300'}],'On devine that setting elements of a |°|-closed support to zero gives a general quotient, without deleting all their faces.','Define the quotient on the eventual support lattice/disjunctor and prove which magasin structure descends; for actual set figures restriction to a subset supplies the model.')
